        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 327,
      "author": {
        "id": 1954750
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T12:20:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wanted to imply that this function (`GenerateKey`) should be called only if it\u0027s not running on GSI (because we\u0027d want to skip the test this function is called for, and this function offers no mechanism for notifying the caller that we want to skip).\n\nI\u0027ve now added a comment which hopefully makes that more explicit?",
      "parentUuid": "cc3db696_4a9a43d5",
      "revId": "5d4876fac6b68e8f29ffa08ea418e63a0112c180",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd1a9123_e7308600",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/vts/functional/KeyMintAidlTestBase.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 327,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T12:40:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It does make it more explicit, but aren\u0027t there loads of places that call `GenerateKey` that don\u0027t currently/yet have any GSI checks?\n\n(E.g. what happens if you locally hack `is_gsi_image()` to return `true` and run the VTS tests?)",
      "parentUuid": "10b42323_097cefe2",
      "revId": "5d4876fac6b68e8f29ffa08ea418e63a0112c180",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
